Drop -Werror from the accept() probe's CMAKE_FLAGS.

CMAKE_FLAGS entries are passed to the nested cmake, not to the compiler, so this
-Werror never reached the probe and was silently ignored by cmake < 4.4.0. CMake
4.4.0 validates -W<category> and fails with:

    CMake Error: The warning category "error -DCMAKE_CXX_LINK_EXECUTABLE=..." is not known.

Fixed upstream in mongo-c-driver 2.x; we are pinned to 1.28.0 because
mongo-cxx-driver 4.x is a breaking API change.

--- a/src/libmongoc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/libmongoc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -433,7 +433,7 @@
 
    TRY_COMPILE (RES ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}
    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/accept_test${VAR}.c CMAKE_FLAGS
-   "-Werror -DCMAKE_CXX_LINK_EXECUTABLE='echo not linking now...'" OUTPUT_VARIABLE LOG2)
+   "-DCMAKE_CXX_LINK_EXECUTABLE='echo not linking now...'" OUTPUT_VARIABLE LOG2)
 
    if (RES)
       message (
